#!spectest
# mode: run
# adjudicator: production-v1
# since: spec-v0.1
# features: [move, callable]
# doc: |
#   RV-F #15 (single-owner Callable, REJECT direction — the enum-variant position).
#   A bare `Callable` identifier passed to an enum-variant constructor (here the
#   prelude `Some(f)`) is an implicit copy of a single-owner value —
#   E_MoveWithoutOperator (write `!f` / `f.clone()`). This pins the enum-variant
#   arm of production's single-owner-init carve-out.
#
#   adjudicator: production-v1 — ELABORATE-stage reject (GGDEF-SKIP on the ggdef
#   run-surface lane; C/LLVM affirm error[E_MoveWithoutOperator] at build).
#
#   KNOWN SELF-HOST GAP (filed, TODO.md): the self-host does not treat `Callable`
#   as single-owner, so it ACCEPTS this enum-variant init — the self-host lane
#   MISMATCHes. The expected verdict is what the language SHOULD do (reject); the
#   fixture EXPOSES the gap.
# expect:
#   exit: 1
#   stdout: ""
#   reject: E_MoveWithoutOperator
#!end

void main():
    Callable[int(int)] f = (n): n * 2
    Option[Callable[int(int)]] o = Some(f)
    print("x")
